---
title: Sustainability
seoDescription: How Hotel Atlantis tries to sit lightly in De Pijp, and what we ask of guests.
---
## A city hotel, on purpose

The greenest thing about a stay here is where it is. The Albert Cuypmarkt is around the corner, the Museumplein is five minutes away on the tram, and the historic centre about a quarter of an hour on foot. Almost nothing a guest comes to Amsterdam for needs a car, and we would rather point you at a tram stop than a car park.

## In the building

An old building on the Ceintuurbaan is not a new one, and we work with what it is. Lighting through the hotel is LED, and the heating is zoned so that empty floors are not warmed all day.

## Housekeeping

Rooms are not made up with fresh linen every day as standard. Leave the card on the bed and we will change it; leave it where it is and we will not. Bathroom amenities are refillable rather than single-use miniatures.

## What we ask of guests

Separate your waste using the bins on each floor, and tell us if something is dripping, running or stuck on. A tap left running overnight in a building this size undoes a good deal of the rest of this page.
